1.  Q: How to get the first ELTreeItem in the tree?
    A: Don't forget about Items property of ELTree. You can access all the items
       with the Items.Item[index] property.

2.  Q: How to clear the whole tree?
    A: There is a public method Clear in the TELTreeItems.

3.  Q: Why is adding 1000 items so slow?
    A: When you do some time-consuming procedure like adding lots of items or
       deleting lots of items, don't forget to make such thing:

       ELTree.IsUpdating:=true; // this prevents redrawing
       YourMethodToAdd1000Items;
       ELTree.IsUpdating:=false; // redraw the tree now!

4.  Q: I set IsUpdating, do something, but the tree doesn't redraw itself.
       What's up?
    A: When you set IsUpdating to True, the internal update counter
       increments. The tree is redrawn when the counter is 0. So you should do
       IsUpdating:=false after you have set it to True. 

5.  Q: Why is the scrolling so slow and flickering?
    A: Yes, this can happen on slow computers. Turning off ScrollTracikng will
       speed up scrolling.

6.  Q: Is it possible to draw an image in one of the listview cells of the
       ElTree grid (not just for the nodes of the treeview part?)
    A: Sure. First you have to mark the cells as owner-drawn. If
       OwnerDrawByColumn property is true, then the header section's style
       defines, whether the cell is owner drawn. If OwnerDrawByColumn property
       is false, then the text of the cell defines this. OwnerDrawMask defines
       the text, that, when found in the cell, forces the OnItemDraw event to
       be fired. 

       if (OwnerDrawByColumn and (Header section's Style=elhsOwnerDraw))
          or ((not (OwnerDrawByColumn)) and (cell text = OwnerDrawMask))
       then call_event_handler else draw_as_known.

       This behavior is more clear when you take a look at the source code. 

       Other approach is to use CellStyles.

7:  Q: How do I make ElTree behave like a grid?
    A: First, make some fake main column and hide it. Then add the amount of
       columns you need in your grid. To select the cells, and not the rows,
       a) set RowSelect to false. 
       b) set MultiSelect to false (if needed). 
       c) set SelectColumn to the index of the column you want to select. 
          When the user clicks the cell or presses the arrow key, you will need
          to change the value of this parameter. 
       d) enjoy :).

       You will access the cell's data as Items[Row].ColumnText[Column]. This is 
       quick and easy. BTW forget about main tree column: it is hidden and
       nobody will ever see or use it. 
       
8.  Q: How do I draw the item's line with some color?
    A: use CellStyles. Set Item.UseStyles to true, and see the help file :).
       The demo project ElIniEdit uses CellStyles to provide custom coloring.

9.  Q: The text bottom is cut, when HorizontalLines is false. A bug!
    A: 1) Version 2.02 fixes this problem for a common situations. Although it 
          cannot remove all the problems, as some Cell Style can define the
          font size as 72 ;)
       2) Try to set Font.Height as POSITIVE value. Then internal font leading
          is counted.       


